So it degrades honestly while you're setting up rather than dumping JSON at you.
What it does once configured: 302 → Google → callback exchanges the code → looks up the account by email → creates one if it's new (handle derived from the email prefix) → redirects back with the API key → page stores it, strips it from the URL. Existing accounts matched by email log straight in instead of duplicating.
Also wired: state.apiKey now rides along, so signed-in users are identified by their real handle rather than the random pog_xxxx blob — and claim_owner in the API will move an existing anonymous profile onto the account if you sign up after already sculpting.
